left to right direction
class "Job (processing.models)" as J <<ORM>> $PROC {
 + id: UUID
 + asset_id: UUID
 + source: dict
 + operations: list
 + status: str
 + current_attempt_id: UUID
 + outputs: list
}
class "Attempt (processing.models)" as A <<ORM>> $PROC {
 + id: UUID
 + job_id: UUID
 + attempt_number: int
 + state: str
 + lease_token: UUID | None
}
class "Claim (processing.lifecycle)" as C <<frozen dataclass>> $PROC {
 + job_id: UUID
 + attempt_id: UUID
 + lease_token: UUID
 + owner_id: UUID
 + source: dict
 + operations: list
 + source_url: str
 + source_url_expires_at: datetime
 + deadline_at: datetime
}
class "AttemptTask (messaging_models)" as B <<ORM>> $PROC {
 + attempt_id: UUID
 + task_name: str
}
J "1" -- "1..*" A : job_id
J "0..1" --> "1" A : current_attempt_id
C ..> J : execution snapshot
C ..> A : token authority
A "1" -right- "0..1" B
legend bottom
+ public; - internal by Python convention; underlined = class/module scope.
Selected Mapped[T] fields shown as T. Claim's field bindings are frozen; source/operations remain mutable dict/list (source_url has repr=False).
Claim is returned by processing.lifecycle.claim, not an entity method. Supervisor.work holds this snapshot.
AttemptTask.task_name is SQL UNIQUE. Functions/adapters: W3-19; retry/lease functions: W3-21.
endlegend

